  "material_conclusion": "The loss-avoidance premise reversed across windows. In Design, Employment Situation days had higher median return and a lower negative-return rate than same-weekday controls, directly contradicting the cash-veto thesis. Validation showed an adverse median-return and negative-rate gap, but Fisher p=0.18841585, drawdown breadth only 1/2 years, and top-one/top-three loss concentration of 32.96%/66.31% failed the frozen independence and breadth gates. The complete-day veto therefore lacks repeatable predictive support.",
  "uncertainty": [
    "The complete UTC day is a coarse window around the 08:30 Eastern release and does not causally isolate labor news from other information arriving that day.",
